    <statement><p>The expression <m>\displaystyle{\ \sqrt[3]{\sqrt{{729} x^5}} \ }</m> equals
<m>\displaystyle{\ nx^r }</m></p>
<p>where <m>\ n</m>, the leading coefficient, is: <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>and <m>\ r</m>, the exponent of <m>\ x</m>, is:  <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{5}{6}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{gathered}\sqrt[3]{\sqrt{{729} x^5}} 
= \sqrt[3]{\sqrt{{3}^6 x^5}}
= \big( ({3}^6 x^5)^{1/2}\big)^{1/3}\\
= ({3}^{6/2}x^{5/2})^{1/3} 
= {3}^{6/6} x^{5/6} 
= {3} x^{5/6} \end{gathered}}</m></p>
</solution>
